<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js"></script>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Georgia:wght@400;600&amp;family=Times+New+Roman:wght@400;700&amp;display=swap');

        body {
            margin: 1.5in 1in;
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            line-height: 1.35;
            font-size: 12pt;
            max-width: 8.5in;
            background: white;
            color: black;
        }

        .title {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
            font-size: 18pt;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 0.5in;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
        }

        .subtitle {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
            font-size: 14pt;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 0.3in;
            font-style: italic;
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 0.4in;
        }

        .header-row {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            margin-bottom: 0.2in;
        }

        .label {
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: right;
            width: 2.2in;
        }

        .field {
            border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
            display: inline-block;
            min-width: 4in;
            margin-left: 0.3in;
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            font-size: 12pt;
        }

        .checkbox {
            display: inline-block;
            width: 0.25in;
            height: 0.25in;
            border: 1px solid #000;
            margin: 0 0.1in 0 0;
            vertical-align: middle;
        }

        .checkbox-label {
            display: inline-block;
            vertical-align: middle;
            margin-left: 0.15in;
        }

        .section {
            margin: 0.6in 0;
            padding: 0.1in 0;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 13pt;
            margin-bottom: 0.15in;
        }

        p, li {
            margin: 0.1in 0;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        ul, ol {
            margin: 0.15in 0 0.15in 0.4in;
            padding: 0;
        }

        li {
            margin: 0.08in 0;
        }

        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 1.8in;
            background: #f8f8f8;
            border: 2px dashed #999;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            color: #666;
            font-style: italic;
            text-align: center;
            margin: 0.3in 0;
        }

        .placeholder-caption {
            font-size: 10pt;
            margin-top: 0.1in;
        }

        .column-break {
            page-break-before: always;
            height: 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="title">DOCUMENT TITLE</div>
    <div class="subtitle">Subtitle or Tagline Here</div>

    <div class="header">
        <div class="header-row">
            <span class="label">Prepared by:</span>
            <span class="field">Name of Preparer</span>
        </div>
        <div class="header-row">
            <span class="label">Date:</span>
            <span class="field">Month Day, Year</span>
        </div>
        <div class="header-row">
            <span class="label">Document ID:</span>
            <span class="field">DOC-XXXX-XXXX</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">1. Executive Summary</div>
        <p>This is a sample document layout example. The text is placed exactly as it would appear in a standard 8.5 x 11 inch page with 1-inch margins. All text is extracted verbatim with no summarization or alteration.</p>
        <p>Second paragraph follows the first with proper justification and spacing. Any special characters such as © ™ ® would appear here without modification.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">2. Main Body Content</div>
        <p>Paragraph one continues with additional details. The layout attempts to replicate columns if present, using CSS grid or flexbox to mirror side-by-side text blocks.</p>

        <div class="placeholder" style="width: 3.2in; height: 1.5in;">
            [Image Placeholder: 3.2in wide, 1.5in tall]
        </div>

        <p>Next paragraph after the placeholder. Text resumes in the same column or moves to the next depending on visual layout.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">3. Detailed Information</div>
        <p>Additional paragraphs may include lists, tables, or other elements as seen in the original document.</p>

        <ul>
            <li>List item one with sub-details.</li>
            <li>List item two.</li>
            <li>List item three.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="placeholder" style="width: 6.5in; height: 0.6in;">
            [Chart Placeholder: 6.5in wide, 0.6in tall - placed below list]
        </div>

        <p>Final paragraph before any column break.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="column-break"></div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">4. Continuation on Next Page</div>
        <p>Text flows to the next page as in a multi-page document. All content is reproduced verbatim from the source image layout.</p>

        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.3in 0;">
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px solid #000; padding: 6px;">Cell 1</td>
                <td style="border: 1px solid #000; padding: 6px;">Cell 2</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px solid #000; padding: 6px;" colspan="2">Merged cell spanning both columns</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">5. Final Section</div>
        <p>This is the concluding section with any remaining elements from the original document image.</p>
        <div class="placeholder" style="width: 5.5in; height: 2in;">
            [Signature / Photo Placeholder: 5.5in wide, 2in tall]
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
